{
  "id": "should-advice",
  "type": "grammar",
  "level": "B1",
  "title": "Should for advice",
  "title_es": "Dar consejos con should",
  "icon": "light-bulb",
  "description": "Cómo dar consejos y recomendaciones.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "should",
      "title": "should / shouldn't",
      "title_es": "Deberías / no deberías",
      "use": "Para dar **consejos** o decir lo que es buena idea. Es igual para todas las personas (no lleva *-s*) y va seguido del infinitivo **sin** *to*.",
      "forms": [
        {
          "label": "Afirmativa",
          "pattern": "sujeto + should + infinitivo",
          "example": "You should cut down on fats."
        },
        {
          "label": "Negativa",
          "pattern": "sujeto + shouldn't + infinitivo",
          "example": "Teenagers shouldn't drink energy drinks."
        },
        {
          "label": "Pregunta",
          "pattern": "Should + sujeto + infinitivo?",
          "example": "Should I cut out sugar?"
        }
      ],
      "keywords": [
        "should",
        "shouldn't",
        "I think you should…"
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "en": "You should cut down on fats.",
          "es": "Deberías tomar menos grasas."
        },
        {
          "en": "You should cut out alcohol.",
          "es": "Deberías dejar el alcohol."
        },
        {
          "en": "Teenagers should cut down on energy drinks.",
          "es": "Los adolescentes deberían tomar menos bebidas energéticas."
        }
      ],
      "mistakes": [
        {
          "wrong": "You should to eat more fruit.",
          "right": "You should eat more fruit.",
          "why": "Después de *should* nunca va *to*."
        },
        {
          "wrong": "She shoulds eat more fruit.",
          "right": "She should eat more fruit.",
          "why": "*should* no cambia con *he / she / it*."
        }
      ],
      "tables": [
        {
          "title": "Consejo y obligación en B1",
          "head": [
            "Forma",
            "Significado",
            "Ejemplo"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "should / shouldn't",
              "consejo: es buena idea (no)",
              "You **should** drink more water."
            ],
            [
              "ought to",
              "igual que *should*, más formal",
              "You **ought to** see a doctor."
            ],
            [
              "must",
              "obligación fuerte (lo dice quien habla)",
              "I **must** call my mum tonight."
            ],
            [
              "have to",
              "obligación externa (normas)",
              "Waiters **have to** wear a uniform."
            ],
            [
              "mustn't",
              "prohibido",
              "You **mustn't** smoke in the restaurant."
            ],
            [
              "don't have to",
              "no es necesario",
              "You **don't have to** tip in Spain, but you can."
            ]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "exceptions": [
        "**mustn't** ≠ **don't have to**: *You mustn't eat it* = está prohibido; *You don't have to eat it* = no hace falta.",
        "Para pedir consejo: *What **should** I do?* / ***Should** I cut out sugar?*"
      ],
      "practice": [
        {
          "q": "You look tired. You ___ go to bed earlier.",
          "a": "should"
        },
        {
          "q": "You ___ eat so much junk food.",
          "a": "shouldn't"
        },
        {
          "q": "In my country you ___ pay for tap water. It's free.",
          "a": "don't have to"
        },
        {
          "q": "You ___ drive after drinking wine.",
          "a": "mustn't"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
